    {
      "id": "library/arxiv-2007.10190v2/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Asymptotic expansions in perturbative quantum field theory",
      "pageStart": 1,
      "pageEnd": 2,
      "target": "../sections/sec-001-11-asymptotic-expansions-in-perturbative-quantum.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Perturbative expansions in quantum field theories are often\nmathematically defined but typically lead to factorially divergent\nformal power series. Important examples are the perturbative\nexpansions of the partition function of 3-dimensional manifolds (with,\nor without boundary) in complex Chern-Simons theory with arbitrary\ngauge group. For instance, in~\\cite{GLM} it was shown that the LMO\ninvariant of a 3-manifold (which is the perturbative expansion of the\nWitten-Reshetikhin-Turaev invariant at the trivial flat collection and\narbitrary gauge group), is a Gevrey-1 formal power series, that is",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/arxiv-2007.10190v2/blocks/prose-sec-front-matter",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Front matter",
      "pageStart": 1,
      "pageEnd": 1,
      "target": "../sections/sec-front-matter.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "THE RESURGENT STRUCTURE OF QUANTUM KNOT INVARIANTS\nSTAVROS GAROUFALIDIS, JIE GU, AND MARCOS MARI˜NO\nAbstract. The asymptotic expansion of quantum knot invariants in complex Chern-Simons\ntheory gives rise to factorially divergent formal power series. We conjecture that these series\nare resurgent functions whose Stokes automorphism is given by a pair of matrices of q-series\nwith integer coeﬃcients, which are determined explicitly by the fundamental solutions of a\npair of linear q-diﬀerence equations. We further conjecture that for a hyperbolic knot, a dis-\ntinguished entry of those matrices equa",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/arxiv-2007.10190v2/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Resurgence in complex Chern-Simons theory",
      "pageStart": 2,
      "pageEnd": 4,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-12-resurgence-in-complex-chern-simons-theory.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In what follows, we will identify the partition function of complex\nChern-Simons theory with the state integral of Andersen-Kashaev\nin~\\cite{AK}, following the ideas of Hikami, Dimofte et\nal~\\cite{Hikami,DGLZ}.  Although this identification has not been\nderived from first principles, it turns out to have a number of\nstartling consequences. We will focus on manifolds of the form\n$M= \\mathbb{S}^3 \\backslash \\mathcal{K}$, where $\\CK$ is a hyperbolic\nknot.\n\nOur goal is to give an explicit description of the resurgent structure\nof the formal power series of perturbative Chern-Simons theory in\nterms",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
    },
    {
