    {
      "id": "library/arxiv-2007.10190v2/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "The equation x-2(1-x)3=1 and the 52 knot",
      "pageStart": 5,
      "pageEnd": 7,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-3-the-equation-x-21-x31-and-the-52-knot.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The state integral of the 52 knot is given by Equation (39) below with (A, B) = (2, 3) and\nµ = λ = 0. The critical points of the integrand are solutions of the algebraic equation\nx−2(1 −x)3 = 1 .\n(19)\n6\nSTAVROS GAROUFALIDIS, JIE GU, AND MARCOS MARI˜NO\nThe above equation (which deﬁnes a cubic ﬁeld of discriminant −23, the trace ﬁeld of the\n52 knot) has three solutions ξ1 = 0.78492 + 1.30714 . . . i, ξ2 = 0.78492 −1.30714 . . . i and\nξ3 = 0.43016 . . . , corresponding to the geometric representation, its conjugate and the real\nrepresentation. The corresponding series Φσj(τ) satisfy Φσ2(τ) = −iΦσ",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
