    {
      "id": "library/arxiv-2007.10190v2/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Descendants",
      "pageStart": 7,
      "pageEnd": 7,
      "target": "../sections/sec-005-4-descendants.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "\\label{sec.d}\n\nA key aspect of our study of asymptotic series are linear\n$q$-difference equations which are satisfied for their\ndescendants. This elementary idea leads to descendants of the Kashaev\ninvariant (studied extensively in~\\cite{GZ:kashaev}), of asymptotic\nseries (ibid), of $q$-series as well as of state integrals. In this\nsection we review in detail the story of descendants (or ancestors, as\nthe case may be).",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "not-summarised"
      }
